## 📊 **Database Schema**

### Customers Table
```sql
CREATE TABLE customers (
  id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT uuid_generate_v4(),
  email TEXT,
  phone TEXT,
  country TEXT REFERENCES countries(id),
  first_name TEXT,
  last_name TEXT,
  full_name TEXT,
  subscribed BOOLEAN,
  account_enabled BOOLEAN DEFAULT FALSE,
  gender gender DEFAULT 'NOT_FOUND',
  benefits JSONB,
  default_billing UUID REFERENCES billing_address(id),
  default_shipping UUID REFERENCES shipping_address(id),
  tags TEXT,
  created_at TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE DEFAULT NOW()
);
```

### Billing Address Table
```sql
CREATE TABLE billing_address (
  id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
  customer UUID REFERENCES customers(id),
  first_name TEXT,
  last_name TEXT,
  company TEXT,
  company_id TEXT,
  company_vat TEXT,
  address TEXT,
  additional_address TEXT,
  zip TEXT,
  province TEXT,
  city TEXT,
  country TEXT REFERENCES countries(id),
  created_at TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE DEFAULT NOW()
);
```

### Shipping Address Table
```sql
CREATE TABLE shipping_address (
  id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
  customer UUID REFERENCES customers(id),
  first_name TEXT,
  last_name TEXT,
  address TEXT,
  additional_address TEXT,
  zip TEXT,
  province TEXT,
  city TEXT,
  country TEXT REFERENCES countries(id),
  phone TEXT,
  type TEXT CHECK (type IN ('HOME', 'WORK', 'OTHER')),
  created_at TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE DEFAULT NOW()
);
```

## 🔍 **Customer Relations**

### Data Structure
```
customers
├── email (string)
├── phone (string)
├── country (string) → countries
├── first_name (string)
├── last_name (string)
├── full_name (string)
├── subscribed (boolean)
├── account_enabled (boolean)
├── gender (enum: MALE, FEMALE, NOT_FOUND)
├── tags (string)
├── default_billing (UUID) → billing_address
├── default_shipping (UUID) → shipping_address
├── benefits (jsonb)
└── orders → orders table
```

### Expansion Options
- **`orders`**: Includes customer's order history

